#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:1
msgid "Derived Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:3
msgid ""
"`derived_param` lets you define SME parameters as functions of other "
"parameters during fitting, without adding them to the free-parameter "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:6
msgid "What It Does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:8
msgid "In `solve(...)`, PySME:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:10
msgid "sets the current free parameters,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:11
msgid "evaluates each function in `derived_param`,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:12
msgid "writes the returned value back to `sme`,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:13
msgid "runs synthesis and computes residuals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:15
msgid "So derived parameters are updated at every iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:17
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:29
msgid "`derived_param` is a `dict[str, callable]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:30
msgid "Key: SME parameter name (for example `\"vmic\"` or `\"abund Mg\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:31
msgid "Value: function `f(sme) -> float`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:33
msgid "Rules and Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:35
msgid "A parameter cannot be both free and derived in the same run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:36
msgid "`dynamic_param` is still accepted as a legacy alias, but it is deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:37
msgid ""
"For abundance keys (for example `\"abund Mg\"`), return the **final "
"abundance** you want in the usual abundance scale. PySME applies the "
"internal `monh` conversion for you when writing into `sme.abund`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:41
msgid "Example 1: Tie `vmic` to `teff` and `logg`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:55
msgid ""
"Here `vmic` is never fitted directly; it is recomputed from the current "
"model state at each iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../advance/derived_param.md:58
msgid "Example 2: Enforce fixed `[Mg/Fe]`"
msgstr ""

